2
00:00:23,610 --> 00:00:25,620
(Lee E Dam, Moon Hee, Yoon Ga I)

3
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:35,060
(Jeon Bae Soo, Lee Seo Hwan, Oh Eui Sik)

4
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:57,350
(Happy Anding)

5
00:00:57,350 --> 00:00:59,020
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

6
00:00:59,020 --> 00:01:00,250
(All people, groups, firms, places, and events are fictional.)

7
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:01,450
(Child actors were filmed safely with their guardians present.)

8
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:02,650
(Animal scenes were staged under welfare rules.)

9
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:03,850
(AI-based technology was used in parts of the production.)

10
00:01:28,923 --> 00:01:30,323
The reason Tae Gu refused...

11
00:01:31,333 --> 00:01:33,333
was out of guilt, which I already knew.

12
00:01:36,803 --> 00:01:38,233
Because that's just the kind of guy Tae Gu is.

13
00:01:48,883 --> 00:01:51,153
All right, next up is Kang Tae Gu from Class Two.

14
00:01:51,213 --> 00:01:53,283
The day we first performed together back then.

15
00:01:53,283 --> 00:01:55,183
It's a comedy sketch prepared by Han Jun Seo and his friend.

16
00:01:55,353 --> 00:01:56,353
Let's go.

17
00:01:56,853 --> 00:01:58,053
Hey, wait.

18
00:01:58,653 --> 00:01:59,923
Honestly, more than the show...

19
00:02:02,523 --> 00:02:05,033
- Hey, that is so corny. - We need to do a chant together.

20
00:02:05,493 --> 00:02:06,593
We are a team now.

21
00:02:08,033 --> 00:02:09,533
That moment is what I remember the most.

22
00:02:17,203 --> 00:02:18,213
One,

23
00:02:18,813 --> 00:02:20,843
two, three.

24
00:02:20,943 --> 00:02:22,883
- Let's do this! - Darn it.

25
00:02:24,283 --> 00:02:25,283
I am going to kill it.

26
00:02:25,353 --> 00:02:27,423
(Green Room)

27
00:02:36,193 --> 00:02:38,363
(12th Broadcasting Festival Moonlight Paradise)

28
00:02:55,243 --> 00:02:56,243
They laughed.

29
00:02:57,953 --> 00:02:58,953
The other kids...

30
00:03:00,053 --> 00:03:02,153
looked at us and laughed.

31
00:03:13,433 --> 00:03:15,963
They laughed. They looked at us and laughed!

32
00:03:18,033 --> 00:03:21,103
You are totally a natural on stage!

33
00:03:21,103 --> 00:03:22,873
Look who's talking.

34
00:03:23,243 --> 00:03:24,973
You're hilarious, you know that?

35
00:03:25,673 --> 00:03:27,073
What are you smirking at?

36
00:03:27,313 --> 00:03:30,283
- Get over here. Come on. - You sly devil.

37
00:03:30,913 --> 00:03:32,583
Acting all innocent like that.

38
00:03:32,653 --> 00:03:34,753
- Nice job. - Good work.

39
00:03:35,223 --> 00:03:36,383
You did great.

40
00:03:37,183 --> 00:03:38,193
Great job.

41
00:03:41,893 --> 00:03:45,463
(Driver Kim: Time to go to the essay prep academy. You can't be late.)

42
00:03:45,593 --> 00:03:46,663
Wonderful.

43
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:54,773
Hey, Han Jun Seo.

44
00:03:55,943 --> 00:03:57,913
You're just leaving? Let's eat together.

45
00:03:58,313 --> 00:04:00,913
Yes, let's grab some food. We're a team now.

46
00:04:07,553 --> 00:04:08,753
What are we having?

47
00:04:09,253 --> 00:04:10,653
Hey, look.

48
00:04:10,723 --> 00:04:12,123
What are you guys going to do if I eat it all?

49
00:04:12,523 --> 00:04:13,553
Are you kidding me?

50
00:04:13,893 --> 00:04:15,123
Watch this. Five at once.

51
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:21,303
Hey, watch.

52
00:04:21,463 --> 00:04:23,303
I will order more if needed.

53
00:04:23,363 --> 00:04:24,373
- Just eat. - Really?

54
00:04:26,203 --> 00:04:28,703
Are you kidding me?

55
00:04:28,803 --> 00:04:32,113
- Five of them. - Five? Fine, five it is.

56
00:04:34,113 --> 00:04:35,183
Come on.

57
00:04:35,543 --> 00:04:37,243
- Don't laugh. - I'm watching. Go.

58
00:04:37,243 --> 00:04:39,553
- I'm watching. - Here, watch.

59
00:04:39,683 --> 00:04:42,783
- I'm watching, you punk. - Watch. It's five.

60
00:04:43,783 --> 00:04:46,123
- Watch. - Hey, look.

61
00:04:46,123 --> 00:04:47,453
- Watch. - Yes, go.

62
00:04:48,363 --> 00:04:50,323
Look. Hey, watch.

63
00:04:50,323 --> 00:04:52,363
- Hey, give it to me. Give it. - Let's go.

64
00:04:59,133 --> 00:05:00,943
Jun Seo. Hold on.

65
00:05:03,073 --> 00:05:04,213
You smell like food.

66
00:05:08,083 --> 00:05:10,183
Thank you, Mr. Kim. See you tomorrow.

67
00:05:15,683 --> 00:05:16,883
I am sorry I am late.

68
00:05:22,393 --> 00:05:24,363
Professor Choi called.

69
00:05:24,393 --> 00:05:25,863
He asked if I would consider thoracic surgery.

70
00:05:26,263 --> 00:05:28,963
- And? - I told him I would think about it.

71
00:05:30,103 --> 00:05:31,873
Professor Choi is a nice man,

72
00:05:32,533 --> 00:05:34,703
but he is not the kind of connection that would help our hospital.

73
00:05:35,503 --> 00:05:37,203
Jun Seo, did you have your essay class today?

74
00:05:38,243 --> 00:05:40,243
- How was it? - Pardon?

75
00:05:41,483 --> 00:05:43,713
Yes, it was good.

76
00:05:44,413 --> 00:05:46,053
We covered various discussion topics,

77
00:05:47,083 --> 00:05:49,383
and the other students in my group were quite good.

78
00:05:51,593 --> 00:05:52,593
Is that so?

79
00:05:58,593 --> 00:06:00,763
(Hwaseo High School Photo Album)

80
00:06:00,933 --> 00:06:02,803
Father, this...

81
00:06:02,803 --> 00:06:05,903
Everyone is born with their own place in life.

82
00:06:06,633 --> 00:06:09,173
And I despise people who do not know their place.

83
00:06:09,843 --> 00:06:12,243
I hate the vulgarity of those who cling to others...

84
00:06:12,243 --> 00:06:13,673
without knowing their place,

85
00:06:14,383 --> 00:06:18,113
but I despise the stupidity of forgetting your own place...

86
00:06:18,713 --> 00:06:20,653
and mingling with such people even more.

87
00:06:22,153 --> 00:06:23,223
Do you have any idea...

88
00:06:23,223 --> 00:06:24,893
what that essay class you skipped means?

89
00:06:25,653 --> 00:06:28,963
I took the trouble to help you build connections.

90
00:06:29,093 --> 00:06:30,723
Is it really that hard...

91
00:06:31,433 --> 00:06:33,163
to swallow pre-chewed food?

92
00:06:35,433 --> 00:06:37,673
I am sorry. I will never do it again.

93
00:06:39,803 --> 00:06:40,973
Wait in your room.

94
00:06:41,703 --> 00:06:44,303
You will certainly be punished for what you did today.

95
00:06:50,383 --> 00:06:51,383
Ma'am.

96
00:06:53,113 --> 00:06:55,453
Tell Driver Kim he does not need to come in tomorrow.

97
00:06:56,453 --> 00:06:57,653
Yes, sir.

98
00:07:05,893 --> 00:07:08,303
(Social Groups, Math Competition May 17)

99
00:07:45,233 --> 00:07:47,533
Hey, Han Jun Seo, let's go to the snack bar. His treat.

100
00:07:47,973 --> 00:07:49,003
- What did you say? - Come on.

101
00:07:49,073 --> 00:07:50,073
I only lost to you.

102
00:07:50,143 --> 00:07:51,243
Pay for your own stuff.

103
00:07:52,043 --> 00:07:53,073
I will pass.

104
00:07:53,143 --> 00:07:56,513
Look at him play hard to get. You want to get beat up?

105
00:07:56,513 --> 00:07:57,543
Let go of me.

106
00:07:57,913 --> 00:07:58,953
That hurts.

107
00:08:05,553 --> 00:08:06,753
He means stop acting like you are close...

108
00:08:06,793 --> 00:08:07,893
just because we crossed paths once, right?

109
00:08:07,963 --> 00:08:09,393
What a jerk. Let's go.

110
00:08:13,963 --> 00:08:15,703
I thought that was the end of it.

111
00:08:28,843 --> 00:08:30,243
(Father: New Message)

112
00:08:30,913 --> 00:08:32,383
Here is this weekend's schedule.

113
00:08:32,913 --> 00:08:34,183
Report to me after each one.

114
00:08:34,183 --> 00:08:35,653
(Multiple Mini Interview, 1-on-1 consulting)

115
00:08:35,723 --> 00:08:37,283
(Science Essay Contest, Teacher Kim Min Seok)

116
00:08:54,133 --> 00:08:55,273
Hey, what are you doing?

117
00:08:57,913 --> 00:08:59,073
It started back then.

118
00:09:04,143 --> 00:09:05,513
I just dozed off for a second.

119
00:09:20,733 --> 00:09:21,833
Hey, Han Jun Seo.

120
00:09:22,903 --> 00:09:24,063
Lend me your gym uniform.

121
00:09:25,273 --> 00:09:27,633
Hey, Han Jun Seo. Lend me your recorder.

122
00:09:27,673 --> 00:09:29,873
Hey, Han Jun Seo. English textbook.

123
00:09:29,873 --> 00:09:31,243
Hurry up.

124
00:09:32,113 --> 00:09:33,113
Hey.

125
00:09:33,113 --> 00:09:34,683
- Han Jun Seo! - Han Jun Seo!

126
00:09:36,043 --> 00:09:37,143
I am touched.

127
00:09:40,013 --> 00:09:41,053
Hey, Han Jun...

128
00:09:48,293 --> 00:09:51,063
- Where did he go? - Who? Han Jun Seo?

129
00:09:51,263 --> 00:09:52,263
Yes.

130
00:09:52,363 --> 00:09:54,093
I just saw him heading to the rooftop by himself.

131
00:09:55,433 --> 00:09:57,503
- The rooftop? - Yes.

132
00:10:06,573 --> 00:10:07,713
Hey, Han Jun Seo!

133
00:10:23,663 --> 00:10:24,663
Have you...

134
00:10:25,633 --> 00:10:26,633
eaten yet?

135
00:10:29,433 --> 00:10:31,133
Did you run all the way up here just to ask that?

136
00:10:33,373 --> 00:10:34,473
Well, no...

137
00:10:35,803 --> 00:10:36,973
Not just for that.

138
00:10:38,273 --> 00:10:39,513
I did well on the exam.

139
00:10:39,613 --> 00:10:41,683
I know, you punk. Nobody's saying otherwise.

140
00:10:42,083 --> 00:10:43,613
Show off much?

141
00:10:48,723 --> 00:10:49,953
What are you doing up here all by yourself?

142
00:10:52,453 --> 00:10:53,523
Darn.

143
00:10:54,763 --> 00:10:55,893
Doesn't that scare you?

144
00:10:56,593 --> 00:10:57,823
Goodness.

145
00:11:01,363 --> 00:11:02,363
Right, that reminds me.

146
00:11:05,233 --> 00:11:06,233
Hey.

147
00:11:07,773 --> 00:11:09,843
Let's put on a show together on the school trip.

148
00:11:10,073 --> 00:11:11,343
Just like last time, you, me, and Kim Nam Il...

149
00:11:11,413 --> 00:11:12,473
Why do you keep following me around?

150
00:11:13,573 --> 00:11:15,443
- What? - Just because we hung out once,

151
00:11:15,443 --> 00:11:16,783
do you think we're in the same league?

152
00:11:19,113 --> 00:11:20,313
Know your place.

153
00:11:21,983 --> 00:11:22,983
My place?

154
00:11:26,253 --> 00:11:27,493
Did you just say "know your place"?

155
00:11:31,993 --> 00:11:35,333
Hey, are you mad because I keep borrowing stuff?

156
00:11:35,363 --> 00:11:36,503
Let me make this clear.

157
00:11:36,763 --> 00:11:39,103
I won't waste my life with you guys.

158
00:11:39,833 --> 00:11:41,073
So stop clinging to me.

159
00:11:42,803 --> 00:11:43,803
It is annoying.

160
00:11:52,313 --> 00:11:54,113
And for the finale, we hit them with one more punchline.

161
00:11:54,183 --> 00:11:55,253
Not funny. Next.

162
00:11:55,323 --> 00:11:57,353
Crazy jerk. Why do I need your approval anyway?

163
00:11:57,423 --> 00:11:59,693
- Next. - Hey, what about this one?

164
00:11:59,993 --> 00:12:01,693
It is by a river. A guy is all alone,

165
00:12:01,693 --> 00:12:04,563
- fishing by the river, and then... - Boring already.

166
00:12:05,793 --> 00:12:07,793
He gets a bite. What do you think comes out?

167
00:12:10,533 --> 00:12:12,533
And just like that, everything went back to normal.

168
00:12:20,713 --> 00:12:21,843
Explain this.

169
00:12:22,343 --> 00:12:23,683
(Class Rank: 1 out of 28, School Rank: 2 out of 193)

170
00:12:23,743 --> 00:12:26,083
Does this make any sense to you?

171
00:12:27,113 --> 00:12:28,953
What kind of family do you think we are?

172
00:12:28,983 --> 00:12:32,023
How dare you let someone stand above you?

173
00:12:32,053 --> 00:12:34,223
(Class Rank: 1 out of 28, School Rank: 2 out of 193)

174
00:12:34,723 --> 00:12:37,023
Do you know what I despise the most?

175
00:12:37,223 --> 00:12:39,593
It is that defeatist attitude of yours.

176
00:12:40,263 --> 00:12:41,633
When on earth...

177
00:12:41,763 --> 00:12:43,603
are you going to make me proud like your brother?

178
00:12:44,333 --> 00:12:46,203
- Having ambition... - Father was as terrifying as ever,

179
00:12:46,873 --> 00:12:48,773
and the words coming out of his mouth...

180
00:12:49,303 --> 00:12:52,373
made no sense to me at all.

181
00:12:52,643 --> 00:12:53,973
You should learn to be grateful.

182
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:56,783
How pathetic.

183
00:13:04,053 --> 00:13:05,423
I will not let it slide a second time.

184
00:13:06,493 --> 00:13:07,493
Leave.

185
00:13:13,493 --> 00:13:16,763
Never forget who you are.

186
00:13:23,473 --> 00:13:25,773
(Hwaseo High School Trip)

187
00:13:31,083 --> 00:13:32,613
I said hair was free choice.

188
00:13:34,513 --> 00:13:36,153
Did I say your face was free choice?

189
00:13:38,793 --> 00:13:40,793
Who told you to look like that?

190
00:13:41,053 --> 00:13:42,163
I am sorry!

191
00:13:44,363 --> 00:13:45,363
I am sorry.

192
00:13:48,363 --> 00:13:51,103
More than miserable, I felt lonely.

193
00:13:53,333 --> 00:13:54,603
Why is my life like this?

194
00:13:54,803 --> 00:13:56,043
That won't do. Push-up position.

195
00:13:56,573 --> 00:13:58,003
How long do I have to endure this?

196
00:14:03,043 --> 00:14:06,213
If I hold out, will it ever end?

197
00:14:10,023 --> 00:14:12,123
Hey, how many times have you been dumped now?

198
00:14:12,723 --> 00:14:13,823
Twenty-seven times.

199
00:14:14,353 --> 00:14:15,363
Hey.

200
00:14:15,423 --> 00:14:16,863
Usually, after being rejected that much,

201
00:14:16,923 --> 00:14:17,993
wouldn't you just give up?

202
00:14:18,693 --> 00:14:21,393
Hey, I am not just anyone.

203
00:14:22,603 --> 00:14:26,503
Put some back into it. Drive it in like this.

204
00:14:26,503 --> 00:14:30,103
- Harder. - I am doing it!

205
00:14:30,403 --> 00:14:32,513
- Darn it. - You put zero effort into this.

206
00:14:32,513 --> 00:14:35,113
- Why does it keep... - What is with him? Hey.

207
00:14:35,543 --> 00:14:37,183
- I cannot do this to Lee Na Yeon... - Where are you going?

208
00:14:37,213 --> 00:14:39,013
I feel too bad for Lee Na Yeon to do this.

209
00:14:39,113 --> 00:14:41,383
What is your problem, seriously?

210
00:14:44,383 --> 00:14:46,623
What? Isn't that the prick?

211
00:14:46,923 --> 00:14:48,123
Where is he going this late at night?

212
00:14:48,223 --> 00:14:50,063
Who knows? What do I care?

213
00:14:55,533 --> 00:14:57,533
Come on, Na Yeon is about to get here.

214
00:14:57,903 --> 00:15:00,173
- Just go already! - Come on.

215
00:15:00,633 --> 00:15:02,773
Let us go back. Hey, my bad. I am sorry.

216
00:15:03,373 --> 00:15:04,843
This guy, seriously.

217
00:15:05,373 --> 00:15:07,273
He is so stubborn. This jerk...

218
00:15:07,343 --> 00:15:09,343
Hey, let us go. Hey.

219
00:15:13,883 --> 00:15:15,523
Wait, is that Jun Seo?

220
00:15:26,163 --> 00:15:27,693
- What is that? Hey. - Hey.

221
00:15:27,763 --> 00:15:28,863
Call Man Sik.

222
00:15:28,933 --> 00:15:31,303
Hey, Tae Gu. Hey!

223
00:15:33,373 --> 00:15:34,773
What do I do?

224
00:15:35,543 --> 00:15:36,773
Hey! Darn it.

225
00:15:39,613 --> 00:15:43,243
Hello? Sir. Well, you see...

226
00:15:43,313 --> 00:15:45,483
The guys... They fell into the ocean.

227
00:15:45,483 --> 00:15:47,053
Sir, what do I do?

228
00:15:47,853 --> 00:15:49,283
Talk to me straight.

229
00:15:49,323 --> 00:15:52,153
- Why did you fall in? - We did not fall in.

230
00:15:52,393 --> 00:15:53,493
We were just going for a swim.

231
00:15:53,553 --> 00:15:54,793
Who are you trying to kid, you punk?

232
00:15:54,853 --> 00:15:57,263
He called me earlier, bawling his eyes out, right?

233
00:15:57,263 --> 00:15:58,893
He said you guys fell in.

234
00:15:59,733 --> 00:16:01,233
Did I?

235
00:16:01,803 --> 00:16:02,803
No way.

236
00:16:02,803 --> 00:16:04,663
They were head over heels in love with swimming,

237
00:16:04,733 --> 00:16:05,933
or something like...

238
00:16:06,033 --> 00:16:07,273
Was that not what I said?

239
00:16:07,933 --> 00:16:09,043
Are you kidding me?

240
00:16:11,913 --> 00:16:13,573
Seriously.

241
00:16:14,013 --> 00:16:15,313
What am I going to do with you guys?

242
00:16:16,843 --> 00:16:19,753
Thirty pages each. Write them properly by the book.

243
00:16:20,483 --> 00:16:21,653
Do not try to cut corners!

244
00:16:35,033 --> 00:16:37,263
Writing lines like we are in middle school.

245
00:16:37,503 --> 00:16:40,333
I like writing lines. You do not have to think.

246
00:16:43,973 --> 00:16:45,673
You are not going to ask why I did it?

247
00:16:47,613 --> 00:16:49,783
We were swimming together, so why ask?

248
00:16:50,513 --> 00:16:52,053
What a weirdo.

249
00:16:53,353 --> 00:16:54,383
Hey.

250
00:16:54,613 --> 00:16:55,853
That is not what is important right now.

251
00:16:55,923 --> 00:16:58,353
I just stood Na Yeon up, so I am about to get dumped, okay?

252
00:16:58,423 --> 00:17:00,223
Would meeting her have changed anything?

253
00:17:00,523 --> 00:17:01,863
Why, you little...

254
00:17:04,663 --> 00:17:05,693
What?

255
00:17:05,763 --> 00:17:08,033
- You want to go? Let's go. - Let us do it.

256
00:17:08,093 --> 00:17:10,663
Do not blame me when you lose teeth and get a bloody nose.

257
00:17:11,233 --> 00:17:12,733
- One punch only. - Don't you cry.

258
00:17:12,803 --> 00:17:13,803
I won't.

259
00:17:13,873 --> 00:17:15,573
If you take this hit and lose two of your teeth,

260
00:17:15,673 --> 00:17:17,803
don't you go running home and crying to your mom.

261
00:17:17,843 --> 00:17:19,173
(Episode 4: Come Back Home)

262
00:17:31,483 --> 00:17:32,923
Are you heading to work?

263
00:17:33,823 --> 00:17:36,163
Let's walk together. I'm meeting friends there.

264
00:17:36,163 --> 00:17:37,463
That way looks really nice.

265
00:17:37,523 --> 00:17:40,233
Let us take that route. That way works too.

266
00:17:40,233 --> 00:17:42,163
Did you eat breakfast?

267
00:17:42,963 --> 00:17:44,703
Do you know that you are totally different...

268
00:17:44,763 --> 00:17:45,933
when you are with your friends?

269
00:17:47,473 --> 00:17:49,273
See? You do not even answer.

270
00:17:50,303 --> 00:17:52,113
Around your friends, you are all smiles...

271
00:17:52,243 --> 00:17:55,113
like a complete goofball, but with other people,

272
00:17:55,183 --> 00:17:56,483
you pretend to be nice on the surface...

273
00:17:56,513 --> 00:17:58,453
while subtly drawing a firm line.

274
00:18:00,013 --> 00:18:03,283
Where did this defence mechanism even come from?

275
00:18:05,023 --> 00:18:06,223
I am annoying, aren't I?

276
00:18:07,293 --> 00:18:09,393
You are wondering why I am hovering around, aren't you?

277
00:18:14,933 --> 00:18:16,563
I am interested in you.

278
00:18:21,203 --> 00:18:22,543
Are we having a staring contest?

279
00:18:25,543 --> 00:18:27,943
Can you not see me? Excuse me?

280
00:18:28,043 --> 00:18:29,243
Can you not see me?

281
00:18:30,683 --> 00:18:31,683
What is with him?

282
00:18:32,483 --> 00:18:34,753
I am leaving first. Do not follow me.

283
00:18:42,123 --> 00:18:43,363
He did not even try to stop me...

284
00:18:45,733 --> 00:18:47,363
What is that? What?

285
00:18:48,063 --> 00:18:50,933
Excuse me. Hey!

286
00:18:52,103 --> 00:18:55,143
- Gosh, look at this. Whose is this? - Move.

287
00:18:55,203 --> 00:18:57,343
Please, just put some pants on.

288
00:18:58,913 --> 00:19:00,173
Who is it?

289
00:19:05,513 --> 00:19:06,583
Jun Seo...

290
00:19:08,113 --> 00:19:09,953
Jun Seo was kidnapped!

291
00:19:22,633 --> 00:19:24,463
Your clothes are ready next to you.

292
00:19:35,083 --> 00:19:37,513
Why are you just sitting here?

293
00:19:39,683 --> 00:19:42,323
How can you eat right now? I told you, Jun Seo was kidnapped.

294
00:19:42,383 --> 00:19:43,583
They shoved him into a long black car...

295
00:19:43,653 --> 00:19:46,923
- and dragged him off somewhere. - Did you see him get dragged away?

296
00:19:48,693 --> 00:19:49,693
Well,

297
00:19:49,763 --> 00:19:52,763
I did not catch it clearly, but judging by the situation...

298
00:19:52,763 --> 00:19:55,733
Then how do you know he did not get in on his own?

299
00:19:57,933 --> 00:19:59,973
- Darn it, cover yourself up. - Gosh.

300
00:20:00,833 --> 00:20:01,843
Wait.

301
00:20:02,703 --> 00:20:04,503
You think he got in on his own?

302
00:20:04,503 --> 00:20:05,813
Be for real.

303
00:20:05,813 --> 00:20:08,213
Someone who splits rent three ways to live in a place like this...

304
00:20:08,213 --> 00:20:09,943
has no business with a car like that.

305
00:20:12,213 --> 00:20:13,213
Could it be...

306
00:20:14,653 --> 00:20:16,353
Because he was struggling financially,

307
00:20:16,623 --> 00:20:18,253
he touched dirty money?

308
00:20:19,853 --> 00:20:22,093
There must be a reason we each have two kidneys.

309
00:20:23,823 --> 00:20:25,023
Jun Seo...

310
00:20:26,833 --> 00:20:28,763
What are we going to do with these sisters' imaginations?

311
00:20:29,633 --> 00:20:31,303
What on earth do you watch at home?

312
00:20:31,433 --> 00:20:33,033
- Am I wrong? - Yes.

313
00:20:33,273 --> 00:20:34,333
Wait.

314
00:20:34,633 --> 00:20:38,573
- Then what is it, seriously? - I guess she wouldn't know.

315
00:20:39,343 --> 00:20:41,113
Jun Seo is different from us.

316
00:20:41,913 --> 00:20:44,983
- He's crazy rich. Filthy rich. - Yes.

317
00:21:30,223 --> 00:21:31,893
The ten years we agreed on are up.

318
00:21:33,793 --> 00:21:35,463
I heard you already announced your disbandment.

319
00:21:37,203 --> 00:21:38,203
Well?

320
00:21:38,603 --> 00:21:40,703
How does it feel to have ruined your life with your own hands?

321
00:21:40,703 --> 00:21:42,003
I still have...

322
00:21:42,843 --> 00:21:43,843
three months left.

323
00:21:46,143 --> 00:21:47,613
Go through the proper steps...

324
00:21:47,913 --> 00:21:49,483
and join the hospital's management team.

325
00:21:49,913 --> 00:21:52,613
It's not as good as three doctors in the family, but we have no choice.

326
00:21:53,053 --> 00:21:54,313
You were always interested...

327
00:21:54,513 --> 00:21:56,853
- in management from the start. - Father.

328
00:21:56,923 --> 00:21:58,593
I'm not interested in working at the hospital.

329
00:22:01,393 --> 00:22:03,823
Do you think it was easy for me to sit back for ten years...

330
00:22:03,893 --> 00:22:05,693
and watch you live like trash?

331
00:22:07,293 --> 00:22:08,963
Either way, I kept my promise,

332
00:22:09,833 --> 00:22:10,963
and now it's your turn.

333
00:22:18,143 --> 00:22:19,773
Was this place always this big?

334
00:22:22,983 --> 00:22:24,643
What's taking him so long?

335
00:22:25,753 --> 00:22:27,253
Leave him be.

336
00:22:28,013 --> 00:22:29,723
They probably have a lot to talk about.

337
00:22:31,383 --> 00:22:33,323
He needs to make a plan...

338
00:22:33,923 --> 00:22:35,393
for his life when he moves back.

339
00:22:39,963 --> 00:22:40,963
Tae Gu.

340
00:22:52,373 --> 00:22:53,373
Hello?

341
00:22:54,713 --> 00:22:57,043
Yes. What's going on?

342
00:22:57,313 --> 00:23:01,313
I couldn't reach Jun Seo at all. What are you going to do?

343
00:23:02,023 --> 00:23:04,083
- About what? - What do you mean?

344
00:23:04,323 --> 00:23:07,223
I told you the rent has to go up if you want to renew the lease.

345
00:23:07,653 --> 00:23:09,893
- You didn't know? - A renewal?

346
00:23:10,463 --> 00:23:12,663
Wait, Jun Seo said...

347
00:23:12,663 --> 00:23:14,163
that you'd definitely renew.

348
00:23:15,463 --> 00:23:16,733
Hold on, what is this?

349
00:23:17,263 --> 00:23:19,073
Jun Seo said that?

350
00:23:35,983 --> 00:23:38,693
I spoke with your friends. They said you never told them.

351
00:23:39,523 --> 00:23:41,423
I'm putting the place on the market right away, just so you know.

352
00:23:47,533 --> 00:23:52,103
(Kang Tae Gu)

353
00:23:57,573 --> 00:23:58,603
I'll get going.

354
00:24:00,473 --> 00:24:01,773
Don't forget...

355
00:24:02,543 --> 00:24:03,643
who you are.

356
00:24:10,153 --> 00:24:12,193
I spent ten years running away for dear life.

357
00:24:15,293 --> 00:24:16,593
And I'm still here.

358
00:24:23,033 --> 00:24:24,063
Back here again.

359
00:24:27,173 --> 00:24:29,503
They say he gets summoned once a year...

360
00:24:29,503 --> 00:24:31,343
for his grandfather's memorial service.

361
00:24:31,343 --> 00:24:34,173
I knew there was something classy about him.

362
00:24:34,173 --> 00:24:37,713
He's just completely different from Tae Gu and Nam Il.

363
00:24:38,013 --> 00:24:41,453
Because he only ate expensive things growing up,

364
00:24:41,513 --> 00:24:43,523
his skin radiates from within.

365
00:24:44,353 --> 00:24:45,453
Let me see.

366
00:24:45,523 --> 00:24:48,723
Maybe I should take care of my skin a little bit too.

367
00:24:48,893 --> 00:24:50,463
It's been so dry and flaky lately.

368
00:24:50,763 --> 00:24:52,463
I really need to see a dermatologist.

369
00:24:53,033 --> 00:24:54,393
It's so expensive, though.

370
00:24:54,463 --> 00:24:56,933
It's not like I'm earning any money right now.

371
00:24:57,003 --> 00:24:58,833
Maybe I should look for a part-time job.

372
00:24:58,933 --> 00:25:01,803
Are you listening to me? Am I talking to myself?

373
00:25:02,773 --> 00:25:03,843
Same as always.

374
00:25:04,043 --> 00:25:07,373
Talking to myself and answering myself.

375
00:25:08,673 --> 00:25:10,043
Still no word from Jun Seo?

376
00:25:10,483 --> 00:25:11,483
Yes.

377
00:25:11,943 --> 00:25:13,683
He probably slept there and went straight to work.

378
00:25:14,413 --> 00:25:15,753
Isn't this his first time sleeping out?

379
00:25:20,753 --> 00:25:21,993
You know, Jun Seo...

380
00:25:23,063 --> 00:25:24,563
Not telling us about renewing this place...

381
00:25:24,623 --> 00:25:25,863
Don't you have that interview today?

382
00:25:26,993 --> 00:25:29,133
Then shut it and eat up, you jerk.

383
00:25:29,833 --> 00:25:31,263
Your brother-in-law set it up, right?

384
00:25:31,263 --> 00:25:32,303
You cannot be late.

385
00:25:34,533 --> 00:25:35,773
You haven't ironed that yet, have you?

386
00:25:50,753 --> 00:25:53,093
(Where are you?)

387
00:26:18,543 --> 00:26:19,553
Excuse me.

388
00:26:23,423 --> 00:26:24,423
Can we talk?

389
00:26:40,903 --> 00:26:42,103
I have a favour to ask.

390
00:26:44,803 --> 00:26:45,913
About that day...

391
00:26:47,713 --> 00:26:48,843
Please keep it a secret.

392
00:26:49,883 --> 00:26:51,083
Especially from the guys.

393
00:26:57,323 --> 00:27:00,623
If they find out, they will never let me hear the end of it.

394
00:27:02,363 --> 00:27:04,063
Once those jerks latch onto something...

395
00:27:04,123 --> 00:27:05,163
Don't worry.

396
00:27:06,263 --> 00:27:08,463
I won't tell them, ever.

397
00:27:11,603 --> 00:27:12,603
Thank you.

398
00:27:17,003 --> 00:27:18,403
And I am sorry for getting angry that day.

399
00:27:18,743 --> 00:27:19,743
No.

400
00:27:21,243 --> 00:27:22,313
Don't be.

401
00:27:23,183 --> 00:27:25,913
It was my fault for crossing the line.

402
00:27:28,583 --> 00:27:29,583
No.

403
00:27:30,083 --> 00:27:31,353
I took it out on you.

404
00:27:32,323 --> 00:27:34,453
I am not usually that much of a jerk.

405
00:27:37,093 --> 00:27:38,093
Anyway, I am sorry.

406
00:27:41,033 --> 00:27:42,163
And honestly,

407
00:27:43,333 --> 00:27:44,803
I am really grateful to you.

408
00:27:46,003 --> 00:27:47,373
Thanks to you, I feel like...

409
00:27:48,733 --> 00:27:51,673
the guys got to end things with at least one good memory.

410
00:27:55,513 --> 00:27:56,513
Thank you.

411
00:27:58,443 --> 00:27:59,453
Truly.

412
00:28:01,983 --> 00:28:03,383
Of course...

413
00:28:05,023 --> 00:28:06,293
when you kept following us around,

414
00:28:06,623 --> 00:28:08,823
I did wonder what kind of crazy person you were.

415
00:28:21,333 --> 00:28:23,203
Did I offend you?

416
00:28:24,043 --> 00:28:26,413
- I just meant... - It is not that.

417
00:28:32,783 --> 00:28:34,783
I guess I really am crazy.

418
00:28:35,983 --> 00:28:38,783
Ever since that day, I have been reflecting so much.

419
00:28:38,853 --> 00:28:41,753
To stop bothering you, and not get ahead of myself.

420
00:28:41,893 --> 00:28:44,563
I promised myself over and over. I really did.

421
00:28:44,563 --> 00:28:46,933
Even now, begging you not to disband...

422
00:28:46,933 --> 00:28:49,433
is right on the tip of my tongue.

423
00:28:50,363 --> 00:28:51,363
So...

424
00:28:51,963 --> 00:28:53,773
I guess I really am crazy.

425
00:28:56,443 --> 00:28:57,903
Still, I am going to hold back.

426
00:28:59,513 --> 00:29:02,783
Because I don't want to make things harder on you, Tae Gu.

427
00:29:09,453 --> 00:29:10,453
Saying that...

428
00:29:11,183 --> 00:29:13,223
- is basically like saying... - Still...

429
00:29:20,063 --> 00:29:21,063
Even so,

430
00:29:21,833 --> 00:29:25,433
just remember that there is at least one person waiting for you.

431
00:29:25,833 --> 00:29:27,633
Could you just remember that?

432
00:29:39,113 --> 00:29:40,153
All right.

433
00:29:51,123 --> 00:29:52,993
Then can I ask you one thing too?

434
00:29:56,303 --> 00:29:58,733
Why were you crying?

435
00:30:02,203 --> 00:30:03,343
You told me then.

436
00:30:05,443 --> 00:30:06,973
You said you understood how I felt.

437
00:30:10,243 --> 00:30:12,913
What did you mean by that?

438
00:30:17,653 --> 00:30:18,853
Well...

439
00:30:23,623 --> 00:30:24,793
I will tell you...

440
00:30:33,203 --> 00:30:34,933
If you call off the disbandment,

441
00:30:35,843 --> 00:30:38,703
I will tell you then.

442
00:30:59,493 --> 00:31:01,593
You are relentless.

443
00:31:03,103 --> 00:31:04,103
Fine.

444
00:31:04,663 --> 00:31:05,663
See you around.

445
00:31:06,103 --> 00:31:08,433
Wait, no, I did not mean we should meet again.

446
00:31:10,303 --> 00:31:12,403
- I'm leaving. - Okay.

447
00:31:22,153 --> 00:31:23,683
Gosh, I'm late.

448
00:31:30,793 --> 00:31:32,223
Don't get nervous. You will do great.

449
00:31:32,323 --> 00:31:33,893
You can do this, Kim Nam Il.

450
00:31:34,533 --> 00:31:35,933
(Resume)

451
00:31:36,633 --> 00:31:38,163
I can do this.

452
00:31:41,103 --> 00:31:42,103
Mr. Kim Nam Il?

453
00:31:43,273 --> 00:31:44,803
Hello.

454
00:31:45,143 --> 00:31:47,113
- Yes, hi. - I am Kim Nam Il.

455
00:31:47,473 --> 00:31:49,813
- Have a seat. - Yes, thank you.

456
00:31:54,353 --> 00:31:56,223
I've heard so much about you from my brother-in-law.

457
00:31:56,283 --> 00:31:57,723
He said you were his closest junior colleague.

458
00:31:57,983 --> 00:31:58,983
Right.

459
00:31:59,293 --> 00:32:00,953
I have heard a lot about you from him too.

460
00:32:01,123 --> 00:32:03,093
He worried about you quite a bit.

461
00:32:04,593 --> 00:32:08,233
Well, anyway, thank you so much for giving me this opportunity.

462
00:32:08,293 --> 00:32:09,663
I will give it my all.

463
00:32:10,603 --> 00:32:13,103
The interview starts at 3pm.

464
00:32:13,103 --> 00:32:14,133
Right.

465
00:32:14,133 --> 00:32:16,643
Before we head up, shall we take a look at your resume?

466
00:32:16,843 --> 00:32:19,773
- Let me look it over for you. - That would be wonderful.

467
00:32:19,843 --> 00:32:20,843
Thank you.

468
00:32:24,043 --> 00:32:27,383
Thirty-four. You are a bit on the older side.

469
00:32:28,183 --> 00:32:31,583
Age is just a number. I get along with people well,

470
00:32:31,653 --> 00:32:34,123
- and I am quick on my feet. - Is this all you have...

471
00:32:34,453 --> 00:32:35,523
for your work experience?

472
00:32:36,723 --> 00:32:39,493
Ten years with Asura?

473
00:32:40,133 --> 00:32:44,503
Well, I worked as a comedian for quite a while.

474
00:32:44,503 --> 00:32:46,703
Friends from high school and I,

475
00:32:46,703 --> 00:32:48,433
- we formed a comedy trio... - This...

476
00:32:48,833 --> 00:32:49,843
Let us take this out.

477
00:32:49,903 --> 00:32:51,503
(Comedy Team Asura)

478
00:32:54,243 --> 00:32:55,343
Why?

479
00:32:57,943 --> 00:33:01,113
In a corporate, rather than someone difficult,

480
00:33:01,113 --> 00:33:02,723
they hate someone who stands out even more.

481
00:33:03,053 --> 00:33:04,883
If you say you are an unknown comedian in your 30s,

482
00:33:05,123 --> 00:33:07,523
they just assume you slacked off for ten years.

483
00:33:08,893 --> 00:33:11,263
There is no reason to take that kind of risk.

484
00:33:12,563 --> 00:33:13,593
Let us take this out...

485
00:33:14,163 --> 00:33:16,933
and list more part-time jobs instead.

486
00:33:17,663 --> 00:33:18,903
What part-time jobs have you worked?

487
00:33:23,443 --> 00:33:24,703
Have you never worked a part-time job?

488
00:33:28,343 --> 00:33:29,483
I am not taking it out.

489
00:33:32,753 --> 00:33:33,753
What did you say?

490
00:33:37,753 --> 00:33:38,953
I said I am not taking it out.

491
00:33:43,293 --> 00:33:45,363
It is my only experience and specialty in life.

492
00:33:45,423 --> 00:33:46,433
Why should I...

493
00:33:47,363 --> 00:33:49,133
leave it out?

494
00:33:58,003 --> 00:34:00,243
Does not being famous mean I was just slacking off?

495
00:34:01,243 --> 00:34:02,983
Does failing mean I did not try hard enough?

496
00:34:09,953 --> 00:34:12,123
I appreciate that you are trying to help,

497
00:34:12,553 --> 00:34:13,593
but even so,

498
00:34:14,453 --> 00:34:16,393
I do not think you have the right...

499
00:34:17,863 --> 00:34:20,393
to dismiss ten years of someone's life so carelessly.

500
00:34:24,703 --> 00:34:25,803
Look, Mr. Kim Nam Il.

501
00:34:26,373 --> 00:34:29,303
- That is not what I meant... - I am going to keep putting it...

502
00:34:30,143 --> 00:34:33,113
at the very top of my resume. So,

503
00:34:34,813 --> 00:34:37,413
I will pretend I did not hear your advice.

504
00:34:40,383 --> 00:34:42,383
I already paid for the coffee.

505
00:34:43,183 --> 00:34:44,923
Sorry for wasting your time.

506
00:35:10,143 --> 00:35:12,143
You do not even have anywhere to go, idiot.

507
00:35:12,143 --> 00:35:13,183
Darn it.

508
00:35:40,673 --> 00:35:42,743
Hey, this is our debut outfit.

509
00:35:42,883 --> 00:35:45,083
What does that matter now? It's over anyway.

510
00:35:45,243 --> 00:35:47,883
- It's just garbage now. - Seriously, man.

511
00:35:47,953 --> 00:35:49,853
Are you money-crazy? Just sell your own stuff, darn it.

512
00:36:03,233 --> 00:36:05,433
- You are back. - You are home early.

513
00:36:07,633 --> 00:36:09,173
How did the interview go?

514
00:36:12,873 --> 00:36:13,873
Bombed it.

515
00:36:14,643 --> 00:36:15,873
I had a sudden stomach emergency,

516
00:36:15,943 --> 00:36:17,683
so I was a bit late, and they told me to leave.

517
00:36:18,183 --> 00:36:20,153
This world is so harsh, Tae Gu.

518
00:36:20,253 --> 00:36:21,913
You should have held it in, you jerk.

519
00:36:21,983 --> 00:36:23,023
You know how it is.

520
00:36:23,223 --> 00:36:25,923
Whenever I get nervous, my bowels give out first.

521
00:36:26,323 --> 00:36:27,923
Come here. Let me plug it up for you.

522
00:36:28,093 --> 00:36:29,993
- Hold on. Stop it, man. - Come here.

523
00:36:30,063 --> 00:36:32,193
Hey, hold on. I got a call.

524
00:36:32,493 --> 00:36:34,233
- It is Man Deuk. - Man Sik?

525
00:36:34,993 --> 00:36:36,863
Hello? Yes, Mr. Jung.

526
00:36:37,963 --> 00:36:38,963
What?

527
00:36:39,973 --> 00:36:41,303
Jun Seo?

528
00:36:42,273 --> 00:36:44,273
Is he not working his shift right now?

529
00:36:46,813 --> 00:36:47,973
So close.

530
00:36:47,973 --> 00:36:49,943
I really thought I could get it today.

531
00:36:50,013 --> 00:36:51,513
It wasn't even close.

532
00:36:51,713 --> 00:36:53,553
How long are you going to keep doing this?

533
00:36:54,013 --> 00:36:55,853
Until I win the giant plushie.

534
00:36:56,723 --> 00:36:58,683
It feels like a haunted house. It creeps me out...

535
00:36:58,753 --> 00:37:00,153
every time I go to the bathroom at night.

536
00:37:00,223 --> 00:37:01,453
- These do? - Yes!

537
00:37:01,453 --> 00:37:02,523
There are too many eyes staring at me.

538
00:37:02,523 --> 00:37:04,163
One would be fine, but there are so many.

539
00:37:04,363 --> 00:37:05,763
I might just throw them all out.

540
00:37:06,263 --> 00:37:07,493
I think they are adorable.

541
00:37:08,463 --> 00:37:09,703
Darn it, where did he go?

542
00:37:10,903 --> 00:37:13,033
This is weird. Skipping work and ghosting us...

543
00:37:13,473 --> 00:37:14,473
like someone irresponsible...

544
00:37:14,733 --> 00:37:16,243
That is not like him at all.

545
00:37:16,873 --> 00:37:18,173
Who is ghosting you?

546
00:37:19,443 --> 00:37:22,413
- What? - Jun Seo? You cannot reach him?

547
00:37:22,713 --> 00:37:24,383
Ever since he went to his parents' yesterday,

548
00:37:24,443 --> 00:37:26,913
he has not been answering his phone. He did not come home either.

549
00:37:28,183 --> 00:37:29,253
He did not come home?

550
00:37:29,653 --> 00:37:30,653
No.

551
00:37:31,353 --> 00:37:32,723
That cannot be right.

552
00:37:33,023 --> 00:37:35,693
- I saw Jun Seo last night. - The number you have dialled...

553
00:37:35,753 --> 00:37:37,693
He came right outside the house.

554
00:37:39,163 --> 00:37:41,363
- Outside the house? - Are you sure?

555
00:37:42,133 --> 00:37:43,803
Yes, I'm sure.

556
00:37:47,633 --> 00:37:49,473
Where would Jun Seo even go?

557
00:37:50,543 --> 00:37:52,803
- The number you have dialled... - Why wouldn't he pick up?

558
00:37:54,473 --> 00:37:58,513
Why isn't he checking his texts? Come on.

559
00:37:58,743 --> 00:38:00,183
I don't get it.

560
00:38:00,253 --> 00:38:02,513
Why come all the way to the house and just leave?

561
00:38:03,283 --> 00:38:04,723
Isn't it obvious?

562
00:38:06,853 --> 00:38:09,563
He left because he couldn't stand someone.

563
00:38:09,923 --> 00:38:12,423
Did you ever apologize to Jun Seo after that fight?

564
00:38:12,493 --> 00:38:13,563
You didn't, right?

565
00:38:15,493 --> 00:38:16,503
Darn.

566
00:38:16,563 --> 00:38:17,963
I told you we shouldn't have brought her.

567
00:38:20,003 --> 00:38:22,503
Hey, didn't you say you were heading to an appointment...

568
00:38:22,573 --> 00:38:24,003
and asked to be dropped off by the main road?

569
00:38:24,073 --> 00:38:25,343
Does my appointment matter right now?

570
00:38:26,473 --> 00:38:27,673
I'll help too.

571
00:38:28,213 --> 00:38:29,513
Just the two of you searching all of Daehangno?

572
00:38:29,583 --> 00:38:30,783
That'll take forever.

573
00:38:31,513 --> 00:38:34,253
Look, we appreciate the thought,

574
00:38:34,883 --> 00:38:36,223
but you really don't have to do this.

575
00:38:36,623 --> 00:38:38,253
We'll drop you off at the bus stop over there.

576
00:38:38,253 --> 00:38:39,893
I like Jun Seo.

577
00:38:42,453 --> 00:38:44,093
So that makes it okay for me to do this, right?

578
00:38:55,533 --> 00:38:57,043
The texture is amazing.

579
00:38:58,143 --> 00:38:59,613
- Here. - Cheers.

580
00:39:12,353 --> 00:39:16,293
(Comedy Town)

581
00:39:18,093 --> 00:39:19,763
Where to next? Where are we going now?

582
00:39:19,963 --> 00:39:22,733
I think we checked everywhere he might go. Right?

583
00:39:22,733 --> 00:39:25,403
- Yes. - What? That's it?

584
00:39:26,003 --> 00:39:27,203
What about people to call?

585
00:39:27,273 --> 00:39:28,773
Doesn't he have any other friends besides you two?

586
00:39:31,343 --> 00:39:32,903
I asked if he has other friends.

587
00:39:33,443 --> 00:39:36,383
Listen, we're all Jun Seo has.

588
00:39:39,443 --> 00:39:40,653
Seriously?

589
00:39:41,153 --> 00:39:43,153
His life is so boring.

590
00:39:43,953 --> 00:39:45,823
Jun Seo's dad's hospital was around here, right?

591
00:39:48,493 --> 00:39:50,393
(Yechan Hospital)

592
00:39:50,463 --> 00:39:52,923
I'm feeling a little intimidated.

593
00:39:54,493 --> 00:39:55,933
This is a private practice, right?

594
00:40:00,733 --> 00:40:01,733
Let's go.

595
00:40:08,173 --> 00:40:10,743
Are hospitals supposed to have this many security cameras?

596
00:40:11,913 --> 00:40:13,513
When is he going to see us?

597
00:40:17,053 --> 00:40:18,083
Excuse me.

598
00:40:18,253 --> 00:40:20,023
The director is in his office, right?

599
00:40:20,823 --> 00:40:24,023
Yes, he's currently preparing for a TV interview.

600
00:40:24,123 --> 00:40:25,523
He'll call you in as soon as it's over.

601
00:40:25,623 --> 00:40:28,093
His own son is missing, and he's doing an interview?

602
00:40:29,563 --> 00:40:31,263
- I can't take this. - Wait.

603
00:40:32,163 --> 00:40:34,603
Can I help you?

604
00:40:37,373 --> 00:40:38,373
Hello, sir.

605
00:40:39,003 --> 00:40:42,213
It's an honour to meet you. I'm Kang Tae Gu, Jun Seo's friend.

606
00:40:42,743 --> 00:40:44,883
- I'm Kim Nam Il. - I'm Go Ji Young.

607
00:40:45,783 --> 00:40:47,513
You're much more handsome...

608
00:40:48,283 --> 00:40:49,313
than on TV.

609
00:40:52,223 --> 00:40:53,753
We haven't been able to reach Jun Seo.

610
00:40:54,223 --> 00:40:56,353
We checked everywhere we could think of,

611
00:40:56,423 --> 00:40:57,723
- and we're worried... - And?

612
00:41:02,833 --> 00:41:03,903
So...

613
00:41:07,173 --> 00:41:09,033
we were wondering if you had an idea where he might be.

614
00:41:09,103 --> 00:41:11,573
I don't. Satisfied?

615
00:41:12,243 --> 00:41:13,573
Please leave now.

616
00:41:13,573 --> 00:41:14,743
(Yechan Hospital)

617
00:41:17,643 --> 00:41:19,213
Excuse me, mister!

618
00:41:22,753 --> 00:41:25,153
I've been listening to you, and you're being a real jerk.

619
00:41:25,383 --> 00:41:27,753
Jun Seo is missing. He's your brother.

620
00:41:30,093 --> 00:41:31,123
Let go of me.

621
00:41:35,093 --> 00:41:36,333
Yesterday, Jun Seo...

622
00:41:38,133 --> 00:41:39,903
told our father something.

623
00:41:41,933 --> 00:41:44,143
Father, Professor Hwang is on the phone.

624
00:41:45,243 --> 00:41:46,243
All right.

625
00:41:50,243 --> 00:41:51,413
Who am I?

626
00:41:59,683 --> 00:42:01,023
Tell me, Father.

627
00:42:03,193 --> 00:42:05,863
- What? - If you're talking about your son,

628
00:42:06,933 --> 00:42:09,193
I gave up that spot ten years ago.

629
00:42:10,663 --> 00:42:12,163
They're my only family.

630
00:42:13,203 --> 00:42:14,533
Over my dead body...

631
00:42:14,633 --> 00:42:15,703
will I ever set foot in this house again.

632
00:42:27,783 --> 00:42:28,913
Do you get it now?

633
00:42:29,253 --> 00:42:31,323
Do you see how pointless doing this here is?

634
00:42:34,923 --> 00:42:35,953
Excuse me.

635
00:42:36,823 --> 00:42:39,693
The director said he's too busy to see you,

636
00:42:39,763 --> 00:42:40,963
so please leave.

637
00:42:46,303 --> 00:42:48,733
It's all a lie. All of it!

638
00:42:49,633 --> 00:42:52,773
On TV, he acts like some noble soul driven...

639
00:42:52,873 --> 00:42:54,643
purely by a doctor's sense of duty.

640
00:42:54,913 --> 00:42:58,043
His own son goes missing, and what? An interview?

641
00:42:59,383 --> 00:43:00,713
I can see clear as day...

642
00:43:00,713 --> 00:43:02,953
how Jun Seo was treated growing up in that house.

643
00:43:03,013 --> 00:43:04,483
It's a miracle he didn't lose his mind.

644
00:43:04,553 --> 00:43:06,453
I would've gone crazy a long time ago!

645
00:43:10,123 --> 00:43:12,623
- Calm down. - Where have you looked?

646
00:43:13,063 --> 00:43:14,063
Everywhere.

647
00:43:14,693 --> 00:43:16,363
Places we've been, places he might go...

648
00:43:16,493 --> 00:43:17,863
We went pretty much everywhere.

649
00:43:18,063 --> 00:43:20,773
What about there? Back on that school trip,

650
00:43:21,373 --> 00:43:22,803
you wrote 30 lucky letters of apology.

651
00:43:32,683 --> 00:43:33,953
What? Wait...

652
00:43:34,213 --> 00:43:36,853
What? Where are you going? Take me with you.

653
00:43:36,923 --> 00:43:38,253
- I said, take me with you. - Hey.

654
00:43:39,223 --> 00:43:42,153
- What? What are you doing? - Safe travels.

655
00:43:44,093 --> 00:43:46,493
- Let me go. - Gosh, that hurts.

656
00:43:48,693 --> 00:43:50,003
I wanted to go with them.

657
00:43:51,433 --> 00:43:52,663
Darn it.

658
00:43:53,903 --> 00:43:55,773
I knew he was having a hard time.

659
00:43:55,773 --> 00:43:58,843
Still, I thought if he lived away from us,

660
00:43:58,843 --> 00:44:00,613
he'd be 100 times better off.

661
00:44:00,873 --> 00:44:02,873
That's why I pretended not to notice.

662
00:44:04,183 --> 00:44:05,183
Hey.

663
00:44:06,343 --> 00:44:08,383
What if he's thinking of doing something crazy,

664
00:44:08,383 --> 00:44:10,053
- like that time? - Do you have to jinx it?

665
00:44:10,053 --> 00:44:13,353
He said he'd rather die than go back home.

666
00:44:13,353 --> 00:44:14,493
It's not that!

667
00:44:15,193 --> 00:44:16,763
We're not going there to find him.

668
00:44:16,823 --> 00:44:18,593
We're going to confirm that he isn't there.

669
00:44:18,993 --> 00:44:20,663
If you're going to talk nonsense, shut it and go to sleep.

670
00:44:21,233 --> 00:44:22,263
You're distracting me.

671
00:44:26,903 --> 00:44:28,333
Why does it have to be so darn far?

672
00:44:47,023 --> 00:44:50,463
(Emergency Dispatch)

673
00:44:52,663 --> 00:44:54,693
(The Perfect Cleaning Experts: Clean Team)

674
00:45:03,673 --> 00:45:05,573
- Oh, no. What do we do? - Hey!

675
00:45:15,913 --> 00:45:16,953
Jun Seo.

676
00:45:18,053 --> 00:45:19,053
Jun Seo.

677
00:45:22,623 --> 00:45:23,623
Hey, Han Jun Seo!

678
00:45:27,893 --> 00:45:29,193
Jun Seo.

679
00:45:29,533 --> 00:45:30,533
Hey!

680
00:45:38,773 --> 00:45:39,773
Jun Seo.

681
00:45:40,773 --> 00:45:41,773
Jun Seo.

682
00:45:47,613 --> 00:45:50,153
- Oh, no. Call for help, quickly. - What do we do?

683
00:45:53,323 --> 00:45:54,393
Nam Il.

684
00:45:55,823 --> 00:45:56,823
Nam Il.

685
00:45:58,563 --> 00:45:59,893
Jun Seo.

686
00:46:00,333 --> 00:46:02,163
- Jun Seo. - Jun Seo.

687
00:46:02,163 --> 00:46:04,033
- Hey. - Hey, you punk.

688
00:46:04,503 --> 00:46:06,903
Jun Seo. Why is this punk's face so swollen?

689
00:46:07,073 --> 00:46:08,703
- Hey! - Hey, are you okay?

690
00:46:11,073 --> 00:46:12,143
Who are you?

691
00:46:13,013 --> 00:46:14,343
Hey, cut.

692
00:46:15,273 --> 00:46:16,883
- Hey, who are those guys? - I'm sorry.

693
00:46:17,083 --> 00:46:18,713
- Who are you guys? - Civilians.

694
00:46:18,813 --> 00:46:21,083
Can't you idiots control the crowd properly?

695
00:46:21,253 --> 00:46:23,123
Why did you let them drag you out?

696
00:46:23,123 --> 00:46:25,883
I thought they were other actors, so I just went with it.

697
00:46:26,323 --> 00:46:27,323
Unbelievable.

698
00:46:28,123 --> 00:46:29,153
- We're sorry. - We're sorry.

699
00:46:31,593 --> 00:46:34,433
- Go. - Do we go?

700
00:46:35,593 --> 00:46:37,063
- We're sorry. - We're sorry.

701
00:46:39,363 --> 00:46:41,133
Unbelievable.

702
00:46:42,133 --> 00:46:43,173
Hey, wrap it up.

703
00:46:51,143 --> 00:46:52,613
Why would I kill myself?

704
00:46:53,153 --> 00:46:54,153
Exactly, you punk.

705
00:46:54,513 --> 00:46:55,783
Who told you to vanish without a word?

706
00:46:56,153 --> 00:46:57,923
Then why did you turn off your phone?

707
00:46:57,983 --> 00:46:59,283
Are you going through an emo phase or something?

708
00:47:00,653 --> 00:47:01,993
Did you really have to jump to that conclusion?

709
00:47:02,853 --> 00:47:04,563
You should have checked who it was before diving in.

710
00:47:04,963 --> 00:47:06,963
I tell you to think before you act...

711
00:47:07,063 --> 00:47:08,063
so many times.

712
00:47:11,533 --> 00:47:12,603
Should I kill this punk?

713
00:47:12,903 --> 00:47:14,173
Yes, let's kill him.

714
00:47:14,473 --> 00:47:15,833
- Come here. Hey. - Hey.

715
00:47:16,273 --> 00:47:18,903
Sit down. You'll catch a cold. Hey.

716
00:47:19,673 --> 00:47:22,113
Sit down. Okay.

717
00:47:22,173 --> 00:47:23,883
- All right. - I'm hot, you jerk.

718
00:47:24,243 --> 00:47:25,443
- You're hot? - I'm fine.

719
00:47:25,513 --> 00:47:26,713
- If you're hot, bundle up more. - Darn it.

720
00:47:37,463 --> 00:47:38,863
Have you been here for two days?

721
00:47:40,493 --> 00:47:41,493
Yes.

722
00:47:44,763 --> 00:47:47,173
Why? Because you hate me?

723
00:47:57,583 --> 00:47:58,643
It's not that I hate you.

724
00:48:00,313 --> 00:48:02,553
I just wanted to run away for a bit.

725
00:48:06,153 --> 00:48:07,623
I knew it was all over,

726
00:48:09,823 --> 00:48:11,023
but when it actually hit,

727
00:48:13,563 --> 00:48:14,793
I couldn't handle it.

728
00:48:16,703 --> 00:48:19,633
So I thought, "Forget it. Let's just bail."

729
00:48:21,133 --> 00:48:23,043
"Then they won't be able to do anything either."

730
00:48:24,973 --> 00:48:26,003
That's what I thought.

731
00:48:26,073 --> 00:48:29,473
- You blockhead. - Total blockhead.

732
00:48:34,883 --> 00:48:35,913
You know,

733
00:48:37,423 --> 00:48:39,523
I have some serious grudges tied to this place.

734
00:48:42,053 --> 00:48:43,163
On our school trip,

735
00:48:43,823 --> 00:48:45,793
you two performed without me.

736
00:48:47,463 --> 00:48:48,493
It was so annoying.

737
00:48:48,833 --> 00:48:52,363
- What? When Man Sik punished us? - After that,

738
00:48:52,363 --> 00:48:54,203
we got beaten to a pulp.

739
00:48:55,503 --> 00:48:57,373
Do you guys remember the day we first met?

740
00:48:58,543 --> 00:48:59,813
- No. - No.

741
00:49:01,673 --> 00:49:02,943
I remember everything.

742
00:49:07,683 --> 00:49:08,883
Looking back,

743
00:49:09,653 --> 00:49:11,483
I think I liked you guys right from the start.

744
00:49:13,423 --> 00:49:16,253
Give me a break. Gosh.

745
00:49:17,863 --> 00:49:19,523
Cringe all you want.

746
00:49:21,333 --> 00:49:23,203
- It is the truth. - Oh, my.

747
00:49:24,533 --> 00:49:26,233
You know, this is something...

748
00:49:27,173 --> 00:49:28,203
I was going to take to my grave...

749
00:49:28,273 --> 00:49:31,003
- because it was so embarrassing. - Then keep it to yourself!

750
00:49:33,343 --> 00:49:35,373
The day we prepared for the broadcasting festival,

751
00:49:35,843 --> 00:49:37,783
I acted like I was just stuck hanging around,

752
00:49:38,743 --> 00:49:39,883
but that was not true.

753
00:49:40,383 --> 00:49:43,623
Darn it, how could you say yes without asking me?

754
00:49:43,753 --> 00:49:45,523
Do you think she will fall for you just because of this?

755
00:49:45,583 --> 00:49:46,593
Whatever.

756
00:49:46,653 --> 00:49:49,193
It is not like I said yes because of Lee Na Yeon.

757
00:49:49,653 --> 00:49:50,763
Oh, really?

758
00:49:50,863 --> 00:49:52,893
You crazy jerk. When did you even memorize her name?

759
00:49:56,703 --> 00:49:59,333
I will contact the school, so just come out.

760
00:50:00,373 --> 00:50:02,703
That day, I had a private tutoring session...

761
00:50:02,733 --> 00:50:03,843
that cost 1,000 dollars an hour.

762
00:50:04,043 --> 00:50:07,043
My dad told me to come out, but I ignored him.

763
00:50:07,913 --> 00:50:09,943
Because I wanted to stay with you guys longer.

764
00:50:11,713 --> 00:50:13,753
I got in so much trouble that day.

765
00:50:15,283 --> 00:50:17,453
Jun Seo, if it was 1,000 dollars an hour,

766
00:50:17,523 --> 00:50:20,653
- should you not have gone? - You nutjob.

767
00:50:21,293 --> 00:50:22,323
Right?

768
00:50:28,393 --> 00:50:29,963
It was my choice, Tae Gu.

769
00:50:35,503 --> 00:50:37,043
I was never smart...

770
00:50:37,903 --> 00:50:39,043
like my father or my brother,

771
00:50:39,913 --> 00:50:41,213
nor was I ambitious,

772
00:50:43,283 --> 00:50:45,613
so I spent my whole life trying to pretend.

773
00:50:48,853 --> 00:50:50,483
Pretending I wanted to go to a top college.

774
00:50:52,783 --> 00:50:54,053
Pretending I was fine being alone.

775
00:50:58,093 --> 00:50:59,163
You were the first...

776
00:51:00,833 --> 00:51:01,933
to see right through me.

777
00:51:06,603 --> 00:51:08,133
People who do not know anything...

778
00:51:09,773 --> 00:51:12,273
keep saying that you ruined my future.

779
00:51:16,513 --> 00:51:17,713
I want to give comedy a shot.

780
00:51:19,113 --> 00:51:21,613
Seriously, for real.

781
00:51:22,713 --> 00:51:24,953
- You want to do what? - Just ten years.

782
00:51:26,083 --> 00:51:27,753
Let us give it our all for ten years,

783
00:51:28,593 --> 00:51:30,123
and if it does not work out, I will walk away clean.

784
00:51:30,923 --> 00:51:31,963
So...

785
00:51:35,333 --> 00:51:36,433
guys...

786
00:51:39,203 --> 00:51:40,403
Do you want to do this with me?

787
00:51:45,203 --> 00:51:47,043
Next is the clinical approach...

788
00:51:47,273 --> 00:51:48,713
for patients presenting with proteinuria.

789
00:51:49,213 --> 00:51:51,843
The evaluation of proteinuria typically begins...

790
00:51:51,843 --> 00:51:55,113
with a positive result on a urine dipstick test.

791
00:51:55,553 --> 00:51:58,183
The dipstick test detects albumin,

792
00:51:58,253 --> 00:51:59,923
and the quantity of albumin is simply reported...

793
00:51:59,993 --> 00:52:04,093
as one plus, two plus, or three plus.

794
00:52:08,893 --> 00:52:09,903
I know.

795
00:52:12,463 --> 00:52:13,473
When you...

796
00:52:14,873 --> 00:52:16,503
asked me to do comedy with you,

797
00:52:20,013 --> 00:52:22,143
it was not really because you needed me.

798
00:52:30,723 --> 00:52:33,723
You reached out to give me...

799
00:52:35,923 --> 00:52:37,293
a way to run away.

800
00:52:50,043 --> 00:52:52,743
Hey, if it weren't for you guys,

801
00:52:54,013 --> 00:52:55,743
I would've died a long time ago.

802
00:53:17,433 --> 00:53:18,503
Tae Gu.

803
00:53:21,873 --> 00:53:23,803
You didn't steal ten years from me.

804
00:53:25,903 --> 00:53:28,143
You gave me ten more years to live, Tae Gu.

805
00:53:50,263 --> 00:53:51,263
I was scared.

806
00:53:56,633 --> 00:53:58,673
I was scared you guys would regret meeting me.

807
00:54:02,173 --> 00:54:03,213
You crazy idiot.

808
00:54:05,013 --> 00:54:07,813
Is that why you acted...

809
00:54:09,383 --> 00:54:12,253
